    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0369" n="1203" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1203"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/170</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-21T18:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 21, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8.51 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8336. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 50. At the request of Foreign Office, I agreed to the following proposal for
                        <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> which was made to Swedish
                    representatives. …<anchor n="1" xml:id="d310-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>If this proposal accepted do you intend have one-half chartered for the United
                    States and one-half to British excepting <hi rendition="#italic">Jemtland</hi>
                    and <hi rendition="#italic">Österland?</hi> It occurs to me if you do, the
                    British may ask that one-half the Dutch boats secured on <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >modus vivendi</hi> be chartered to them and therefore it would be advisable
                    to arrange. You should charter all Dutch boats in American ports and have the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Jemtland</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Österland</hi> return to you for a round trip and let the English arrange
                    with French and Italians for the 100,000 tons Swedish ships which are to go in
                    danger zone. Please give instructions quickly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
